            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for your kind feedback!\r\n\r\nYes, this sometimes bothers me too. Not to the point of becoming dizzy, but still.\r\n\r\nMain problem here is that `WinScrolled` event is not triggered during incremental search (neovim/neovim/issues/21207) but only after it. Which means that 'mini.animate' is notified that scroll should be done after search has started, at which point it knows only about window view prior whole search and window view after user hits `<CR>`.\r\n\r\nAt the moment I am extremely hesitant adding custom mappings in order to \"patch\" any animation behavior.\r\n\r\nI'll try to tackle this problem again. If not successful, I'll add a workaround to documentation; similar to as you suggested.",
